policies.policy:
[AGENCY NAME] has and implements a procedure for developing, implementing, reviewing and evaluating each individual's habilitation or service plan under N.J.S.A. 30:6D-10 et seq. (N.J.A.C. 10:44A-4.3(a)). The plan and monthly documentation of progress are kept in the individual's record (4.3(b)).

Planning is person-centered: the individual directs the process as much as possible, chooses who attends, and the meeting is held at a time and place and in a format that suit them. It follows the planning team definition in N.J.A.C. 10:44A-1.3, and includes the individual, the guardian, the support coordinator, agency staff who know the person and any other responsible persons the individual invites. Rights are not limited because a person has a guardian or family.

The comprehensive IHP contains all 14 elements required by N.J.A.C. 10:44A-4.3(c):
1. a cover page;
2. evaluation summaries;
3. progress on prior goals;
4. the individual's preferences, capabilities and needs;
5. goals;
6. measurable, sequential objectives;
7. the method for each objective;
8. team members and responsible persons;
9. services, with start dates, duration and frequency;
10. barriers;
11. guardianship review;
12. a meeting summary or addendum, where disagreement may be noted;
13. an attendance sign-off; and
14. authorization for approved individual expenses.

The agency's plan must be consistent with the person-centered service plan authorized by DDD and with 42 CFR 441.301(c). Any restriction on a right is not placed in the IHP unless it follows IR-02.
